<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ DAY 1 — OLD TOWN, PAULA REGO, BOCA DO INFERNO -->
<!-- day-count: 3 — Paula Rego museum (half-day) + 25-min coastal cliff walk to Boca do Inferno fills the day -->
<div class="day-block" id="day1">
  <div class="day-header">Day 1</div>

  <!-- walk-over-40: Cascais Old Town is 3 km from Estoril hotel — 44 min walk, ride preferred -->
  <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚕  10 min → Cascais Old Town</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Rick Steves Portugal, Lonely Planet, Fodor's — the historic transformation from fishing village to royal retreat is visible in every street -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <!-- tour-search: 0 qualifying — Cascais walking tours are private/food/hop-on (excluded); ships self-walk -->
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">1.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Cascais Old Town &amp; Harbour</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 Fishing village turned royal summer retreat in the 1870s. Both pasts visible: old cottages beside belle-époque villas, working harbour, 14th-century Citadela walls to the beach. Daily fish auction at the lota — open to visitors.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cascais" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
      <div>⏰ ~1h 30 min</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Largo+5+de+Outubro+Cascais+2750+Portugal" target="_blank">Largo 5 de Outubro</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Cascais_Portugal_1380488243.jpg" alt="Cascais harbour and old town" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="next">🚶 12 min · 🚕  5 min → Casa das Histórias Paula Rego</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Lonely Planet highlight, Atlas Obscura — Paula Rego is Portugal's most internationally recognised modern artist; Souto de Moura terracotta towers echo Sintra -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <!-- tour-search: 0 qualifying — Cascais art tours are private (excluded); ships self-walk museum visit -->
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">2.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Casa das Histórias Paula Rego</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 Museum by Pritzker architect Souto de Moura, twin terracotta towers echoing Sintra's chimneys. Large paintings by Paula Rego — folk tales, Dickens, and the Salazar era: strong women in dark, charged scenes. No booking required.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casa_das_Hist%C3%B3rias_Paula_Rego" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
