      <div>🚫 Closed Monday</div>
      <div>⏰ ~1h 30 min</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Avenida+da+Republica+300+2750-475+Cascais+Portugal" target="_blank">Av. da República</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Casa_das_Historias_Paula_Rego.JPG" alt="Casa das Histórias Paula Rego, Cascais" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="next">🚶 25 min · 🚕  7 min → Boca do Inferno</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Atlas Obscura featured, Rick Steves, Lonely Planet — the blowhole at high tide is one of the most dramatic spectacles near Lisbon -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <!-- tour-search: 0 qualifying — Cascais coast tours are private/hop-on (excluded); ships self-walk along the paved coastal path -->
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">3.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Boca do Inferno</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 A sea cave 2.5 km west of Cascais where the Atlantic erupts through a limestone arch with a deep concussive boom — best within 90 min of high tide. The flat coastal path from town is entirely paved with sea views the whole way.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boca_do_Inferno" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
      <div>⏰ ~45 min</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Boca+do+Inferno+Estrada+da+Boca+do+Inferno+2750-642+Cascais+Portugal" target="_blank">Estrada da Boca do Inferno</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Boca_do_Inferno_01.JPG" alt="Boca do Inferno sea arch, Cascais" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>

