  <div class="day-header">Day 2</div>

  <!-- walk-over-40: hotel to Guincho Beach is 8 km — 90 min walk, ride only -->
  <div class="hotel-first">🏨 FROM HOTEL: 🚕  17 min → Praia do Guincho</div>

  <!-- inclusion-bar: editorial — Lonely Planet top beach, Atlas Obscura, Fodor's — wildest Atlantic beach near Lisbon; Bond film location; Sintra ridge as backdrop -->
  <div class="stop-block">
    <!-- tour-search: 0 qualifying — Guincho tours are surfing/private (excluded); ships self-walk beach visit -->
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">1.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Praia do Guincho</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 Wildest beach on the Estoril Coast — a 1.3 km arc backed by Serra de Sintra, 9 km northwest of Cascais. World-class windsurfing; always windier and cooler. Dress warmly even in summer; tall dunes shelter non-surfers. Parking free.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guincho_Beach" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
      <div>🏛️ Open 24/7</div>
      <div>⏰ ~2h</div>
      <div class="tour-meet"><div>📍 <a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Praia+do+Guincho+Estrada+do+Guincho+2750-642+Cascais+Portugal" target="_blank">Estrada do Guincho</a></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="stop-photos">
      <img src="_build/assets/800px-Praia_do_Guincho_cropped.JPG" alt="Praia do Guincho, Cascais" loading="lazy">
    </div>
