    <!-- tour-search: 0 qualifying — lighthouse tours are private (excluded); ships self-walk around the open headland -->
    <div class="stop-header"><span class="stop-num">3.</span> <span class="stop-name self">Farol de Santa Marta</span></div>
    <div class="stop-row">📒 A squat lighthouse from the 1860s wrapped in blue-and-white azulejo bands, still guiding ships into the bay. The headland around it is an open clifftop viewpoint over the Atlantic; the keepers' houses hold a small lighthouse museum, with the tiled Casa de Santa Maria next door.</div>
    <div class="stop-row">📖 <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Marta_Lighthouse" target="_blank">Wikipedia</a></div>
    <div class="tour-box">
